WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.586
Lab 2 runs the guide's validate
commands on a ring zero test device,

2
00:00:04.586 --> 00:00:06.938
in a test tenant, never production.

3
00:00:06.938 --> 00:00:09.938
The authors haven't run
them, as the page says.

4
00:00:09.938 --> 00:00:14.083
You need Module 1's test tenant and
test device, with the antivirus,

5
00:00:14.083 --> 00:00:19.225
firewall and Attack Surface Reduction
policies assigned to its ring zero group.

6
00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:23.175
Steps one to five run on the
device, in an elevated session.

7
00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:26.270
Step one shows tamper
and real-time protection;

8
00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.888
both should be true, which means enabled.

9
00:00:28.888 --> 00:00:34.203
Step two shows the network protection
and controlled folder access modes:

10
00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:37.975
zero off, one block, two audit,
matching the ring's stage.

11
00:00:37.975 --> 00:00:41.388
Step three shows the firewall
profiles as enforced,

12
00:00:41.388 --> 00:00:44.087
with the values the firewall policy sets.

13
00:00:44.087 --> 00:00:47.757
Step four is Microsoft Learn's
network protection test:

14
00:00:47.757 --> 00:00:51.587
in a browser other than Edge,
open the test site on the slide.

15
00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:56.085
In block mode the connection is blocked
with a notification, event eleven

16
00:00:56.085 --> 00:01:00.362
twenty-six; in audit it isn't blocked,
and the event is eleven twenty-five.

17
00:01:00.362 --> 00:01:04.889
Step five is Learn's command that
lists each rule and its mode:

18
00:01:04.889 --> 00:01:07.787
two for audit, six for
warn, one for block.

19
00:01:07.787 --> 00:01:10.510
On a server, this is the check to trust.
